.TH KUBE-REVAMPED 1 "2026-11-17" "kube-revamped" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kube-revamped \- the Kubernetes context and namespace in the tmux status bar
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kube-revamped
.RI [ options ]
.I command
.RI [ name ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kube-revamped
shows the current Kubernetes context, its namespace and, when asked, its
cluster and user in the tmux status line. It reads them from the kubeconfig
files themselves, every file in KUBECONFIG in order, so the status line needs
no kubectl. The entry point
.B kube-revamped.tmux
runs
.B apply
once when tmux loads the plugin, which binds the context menu key and every
other key that is set, in one tmux call, and replaces the placeholders
#{kube}, #{kube_context} and #{kube_namespace} in status-left and
status-right with calls to
.BR status .
.PP
A status call prints the stored reading at once. When that reading is older
than the interval it starts one reading in the background, so the status line
never waits. The namespace menu, switching and the probes call kubectl, each
probe with a 2 second request timeout and stopped after 5 seconds.
.PP
A key with nothing to show says why in a tmux message. Run with no command
on a terminal, the tool offers a menu.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B apply
Bind the keys and replace the status placeholders now.
.TP
.B list
Print every tmux command apply would send, one per line, and change nothing.
.TP
.B status
Print one placeholder from the stored reading: kube, context or namespace. The status line runs it, and it starts a reading in the background when the stored one is older than the interval.
.TP
.B refresh
Read the kubeconfig now, store the reading for the status line, run the probes that are on, and say what was found.
.TP
.B use-context
Switch kubectl to the named context, then read the kubeconfig again.
.TP
.B use-namespace
Set the namespace of the current context through kubectl, then read the kubeconfig again.
.TP
.B menu-context
Open a tmux menu of every context in the kubeconfig. Choosing one runs use\-context.
.TP
.B menu-namespace
Open a tmux menu of the namespaces kubectl lists. Choosing one runs use\-namespace.
.TP
.B popup
Open the popup program, k9s by default, in a tmux popup on the stored context and namespace.
.TP
.B doctor
Print one row per dependency: tmux, each kubeconfig file, the current context, kubectl, the popup program, the keys it found bound, gum and the core tools.
A settings row names any setting whose value it does not know.
Exits 1 only when a required tool is missing.
.TP
.B version
Print the version, then the tmux version.
.TP
.B help
Print the help page.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
.B list
prints one JSON object.
.TP
.BI \-\-theme " name"
Colours of the terminal interface:
.BR kodougu ,
.BR catppuccin\-mocha ,
.BR catppuccin\-latte ,
.BR dracula ,
.BR nord ,
.BR gruvbox ,
.B tokyo\-night
or
.BR mono .
The default is
.BR kodougu .
.TP
.BI \-\- setting " value"
Any tmux option below, named with dashes, such as
.B \-\-interval
or
.BR \-\-show\-cluster .
It also takes the form
.IR \-\-setting = value ,
and outranks the environment and the tmux option. Given to
.BR apply ,
it rides on every binding, every menu item and every status call.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B KUBECONFIG
The kubeconfig files, separated by colons. The default is
.IR ~/.kube/config .
.TP
.BI KUBE_REVAMPED_ SETTING
Any tmux option below in capitals, such as
.BR KUBE_REVAMPED_INTERVAL .
It outranks the tmux option.
.TP
.B KUBE_REVAMPED_THEME
The theme when
.B \-\-theme
is not given.
.TP
.B KUBE_REVAMPED_ACCENT
A colour such as #CBA6F7 that replaces the accent of the theme.
.TP
.B KODOUGU_THEME
The theme of every kodougu and tmux-revamped tool, when neither
.B \-\-theme
nor
.B KUBE_REVAMPED_THEME
is set.
.TP
.B KODOUGU_ACCENT
The accent of every kodougu and tmux-revamped tool, when
.B KUBE_REVAMPED_ACCENT
is not set.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Turns colour off in every theme.
.SH TMUX OPTIONS
An empty tmux option means its default. A key set to off binds nothing.
.TP
.B @kube_revamped_menu_context_key
The prefix key that opens the context menu. off binds nothing. The default is M\-k, left alone when someone else holds it.
.TP
.B @kube_revamped_menu_namespace_key
The prefix key that opens the namespace menu. The default is none.
.TP
.B @kube_revamped_popup_key
The prefix key that opens the popup. The default is none.
.TP
.B @kube_revamped_interval
Seconds a reading stays fresh before the status line starts another. The default is 10.
.TP
.B @kube_revamped_color
The tmux style of the segment. The default is #[fg=blue].
.TP
.B @kube_revamped_prod_pattern
A context whose name holds this text takes prod_color. The default is none.
.TP
.B @kube_revamped_prod_color
The tmux style of a production context. The default is #[fg=red].
.TP
.B @kube_revamped_warn_color
The tmux style of a context the kubeconfig lacks, of nodes that are not all ready and of failing pods. The default is #[fg=yellow].
.TP
.B @kube_revamped_warn_icon
The mark after a current context the kubeconfig does not list. The default is a question mark.
.TP
.B @kube_revamped_icon
Text shown before the segment. The default is none.
.TP
.B @kube_revamped_hide_default
1 hides the segment while the context is named default. The default is 0.
.TP
.B @kube_revamped_show_cluster
1 adds @cluster after the context. The default is 0.
.TP
.B @kube_revamped_show_namespace
0 drops :namespace from the segment. The default is 1.
.TP
.B @kube_revamped_show_user
1 adds the user in parentheses. The default is 0.
.TP
.B @kube_revamped_probe_reach
1 runs kubectl cluster\-info on each reading and shows o when the cluster answers and x when it does not. The default is 0.
.TP
.B @kube_revamped_probe_nodes
1 shows ready nodes over all nodes. The default is 0.
.TP
.B @kube_revamped_probe_pods
1 shows the count of pods in the current namespace that neither run nor completed. The default is 0.
.TP
.B @kube_revamped_popup_command
The program the popup runs, with any arguments. It is given \-\-context and \-\-namespace. The default is k9s.
.TP
.B @kube_revamped_popup_width
The width of the popup. The default is 80%.
.TP
.B @kube_revamped_popup_height
The height of the popup. The default is 80%.
.TP
.B @revamped_theme
The theme of every tmux-revamped tool, when nothing else sets one. The default
is
.BR kodougu .
.PP
The stored reading lives in
.BR @kube_revamped_value ,
.BR _value_ts ,
.BR _value_lock ,
.BR _dangling ,
.BR _cluster ,
.BR _user ,
.BR _reach ,
.B _nodes
and
.BR _pods .
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on any failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tmux (1),
.BR kubectl (1),
.BR gum (1)
